{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_05385f8d7a9cc631ed358706d5d7b0605b6d4c2f235b4036d0eddbf945489337"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"v0.6.1 consolidated tools: multi_edit merged into file_edit (edits[] for atomic multi-edit), and four checkpoint tools collapsed into checkpoint (save/rewind/restore) and read-only checkpoint_view (diff/list)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_05385f8d7a9cc631ed358706d5d7b0605b6d4c2f235b4036d0eddbf945489337"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","id":"pg_091478543a095c7787a3a8fd0382bbe7","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/talmetis-labs-aizen-release-notes-v0-6-1-md-997bdd3bbba4-a8fd0382bbe7.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_7e3d2ce5f7f45a50a88ddb7655bcafee"],"title":"talmetis-labs/aizen/release-notes-v0.6.1.md @ 997bdd3bbba4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","id":"pg_3386175d8b9f5942a166d8c5d03cf649","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/talmetis-labs-aizen-readme-vi-md-997bdd3bbba4-d8c5d03cf649.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_af1ed2370aef5a21b22542f20750779e"],"title":"talmetis-labs/aizen/README.vi.md @ 997bdd3bbba4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_38c61cce565629a074ed964da1c14ca3b000211d5a61d1b1ce1384b368e588e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Aizen is documented as a single static binary (~34 MB, ~10 ms cold start claimed) requiring no Node, Python, Docker, or cloud account, targeting Windows, Linux, and macOS."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3af7ab718bcdc97d5b61b3ee2be67fce744197e4861011292aebe22c1f89bfbf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent accepts any OpenAI-style /chat/completions endpoint, including OpenAI, OpenRouter, local llama.cpp/vLLM, or an Anthropic gateway."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6f5411b8c7a55f2cf10ddaf47c3f2a726f7e2e064f1c513f8c7aefbd6ddb9e6a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The sandbox runs commands without inheriting API keys, denies network by default, and enforces filesystem policy via Landlock+seccomp on Linux and Seatbelt on macOS; Windows uses Job-Object containment and reports 'partial'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7bc1e401d59be4d25fc94a0d810f93d5808a5f468b6e6dcb30c793f993ad1c77"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A 'Pantheon' of seven capability-scoped sub-agents (argus, metis, daedalus, nemesis, themis, clio, mnemosyne) is fanned out via `aizen workflow`, which synthesizes one answer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8207e6c9419d8e63eb62d7cba4b27e1c2c5bb05ab922b6e5341db7eaccd769cb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent is documented to keep an offline BM25-ranked memory that learns from reuse, plus a persona, a durable 'SOUL' identity, and skills it writes for itself after real work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8849efd66f1205586c9c2b171e884a4def0e1641644273156c58b9e36c22e55e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors sign a CLA once via a bot-comment flow with the exact sentence 'I have read the CLA Document and I hereby sign the CLA'; the CLA grants the maintainer commercial relicensing rights while the public project stays Apache-2.0."}],"claim_ids":["clm_38c61cce565629a074ed964da1c14ca3b000211d5a61d1b1ce1384b368e588e4","clm_3af7ab718bcdc97d5b61b3ee2be67fce744197e4861011292aebe22c1f89bfbf","clm_6f5411b8c7a55f2cf10ddaf47c3f2a726f7e2e064f1c513f8c7aefbd6ddb9e6a","clm_7bc1e401d59be4d25fc94a0d810f93d5808a5f468b6e6dcb30c793f993ad1c77","clm_8207e6c9419d8e63eb62d7cba4b27e1c2c5bb05ab922b6e5341db7eaccd769cb","clm_8849efd66f1205586c9c2b171e884a4def0e1641644273156c58b9e36c22e55e"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","id":"pg_5021d2ad7cfa5d358dd20fc776b4d4e4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/talmetis-labs-aizen-readme-md-997bdd3bbba4-0fc776b4d4e4.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_78784ab34c0f58be8574d58faed5a3e5"],"title":"talmetis-labs/aizen/README.md @ 997bdd3bbba4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3ebecac6d2c2ef8b24fdad97feae964bc5f1f9d5f2bb8fca855285e3a2a5899f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Approval (ask/smart/yolo plus a cmd_guard hard floor) is separate from the sandbox: even approved commands get no secrets, no network, and no out-of-workspace writes where kernel backends exist."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5f074ab5b4c50963369dcd51fc8e9853f5571046eb318299442ed63cfdff038e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sandbox modes are auto (default), strict, guarded, and off; strict refuses spawns rather than downgrading, and unattended runs fail closed unless sandbox.allow_guarded_fallback is true."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6f5411b8c7a55f2cf10ddaf47c3f2a726f7e2e064f1c513f8c7aefbd6ddb9e6a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The sandbox runs commands without inheriting API keys, denies network by default, and enforces filesystem policy via Landlock+seccomp on Linux and Seatbelt on macOS; Windows uses Job-Object containment and reports 'partial'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85b8d7c10e6cdeff1f76449391c3adc777b5bb21bb6ba95008d87c03e8a9178b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The sandbox code is organized under src/sandbox with modules for policy, capabilities, a single runner that builds sandboxed commands, audit logging, and per-platform backends (guarded, linux, windows, macos)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8e621931587e82991be770db96578a73805046d928f621a3aa1aca5ce56e4ee7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The sandbox explicitly does not protect against kernel exploits, an already-compromised user account or machine, secrets placed inside the workspace, or a human approving a harmful command."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3ebecac6d2c2ef8b24fdad97feae964bc5f1f9d5f2bb8fca855285e3a2a5899f","clm_5f074ab5b4c50963369dcd51fc8e9853f5571046eb318299442ed63cfdff038e","clm_6f5411b8c7a55f2cf10ddaf47c3f2a726f7e2e064f1c513f8c7aefbd6ddb9e6a","clm_85b8d7c10e6cdeff1f76449391c3adc777b5bb21bb6ba95008d87c03e8a9178b","clm_8e621931587e82991be770db96578a73805046d928f621a3aa1aca5ce56e4ee7"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807","id":"pg_912e69b7f1235239bed389e58c6be0a4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/talmetis-labs-aizen-docs-sandbox-md-997bdd3bbba4-89e58c6be0a4.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_b5b6b389adf9566c940070ab77081194"],"title":"talmetis-labs/aizen/docs/SANDBOX.md @ 997bdd3bbba4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:25:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5494512d1b9646eebd76d5cf54bcc807"}
